# Sealed corpora whose SHA-256 is recorded in a preregistration must reach the
# working tree byte for byte. Without this, a clone with core.autocrlf=true
# (the Windows default) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, every recorded source
# digest stops matching, and the fail-closed integrity gate refuses the corpus
# on a tree nobody actually modified.
benchmark_web_validation/development/sources/** -text
benchmark_open_source_pairs/cases.json -text
benchmark_open_source_pairs_results/*.json -text
